      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): reject malformed table spans",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram rich-block table rendering could treat malformed HTML table span attributes as valid numbers when assistant-authored HTML contained values like `colspan=\"2x\"` or `rowspan=\"3y\"`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTelegram table span parsing now accepts only complete decimal integer span values and keeps malformed spans as ordinary one-cell table entries. The legacy HTML table fallback also requires a real `colspan` attribute boundary so unrelated attributes such as `data-colspan` cannot hide a later valid span, while preserving valid whitespace-padded span values such as `colspan=\" 2 \"`.\n\nRelated independent bug-family PRs: this is part of a strict external numeric-token parsing wave; each PR is independent, based on `upstream/main`, and has no merge dependency on the others.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTelegram users get table output that matches authored spans more predictably instead of silently expanding malformed partial values into wider or taller cells. Existing whitespace-padded valid fallback spans continue to render as spans.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current head: ed4ad3dd02150d4fbe8e570b13dcff4365fcc4f4.\n- Exact-head terminal behavior proof passed with the current span parser rules from `extensions/telegram/src/format.ts` and `extensions/telegram/src/rich-blocks-html-map.ts`: legacy `colspan=2x` normalized to one cell, `data-colspan=bad colspan=2` still used the real `colspan=2` attribute, `colspan=\" 2 \"` still produced span 2, and raw rich-block `colspan=\"2x\"` / `rowspan=\"3y\"` produced no span while `colspan=\" 2 \"` still produced span 2.\n- GitHub checks passed for head ed4ad3dd02150d4fbe8e570b13dcff4365fcc4f4: `Real behavior proof`, `openclaw/ci-gate`, `check-lint`, `check-test-types`, `build-artifacts`, and QA Smoke CI profiles 1-4.",
